}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, I checked your account and it looks healthy. Your VPN access is on, your account is active, and Duo is set up on your phone. Your VPN connected from Lisbon on each of the last three days, so the problem looks like the hotel network rather than your account. Please try these steps: 1) Open a web browser on your laptop and go to any public website (for example, a news site). If the hotel's Wi-Fi sign-in or terms page appears, accept it, then try the VPN again. 2) If it still won't connect, fully quit the VPN app, restart your laptop, and connect again. Keep your phone nearby to approve the Duo push. 3) If the shared drive still won't open for your presentation, try OneDrive or SharePoint, which often work better on a hotel connection. If the VPN still fails after these steps, please reply with the exact error message and the time you tried, and we will escalate it.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket from Leo Martins (user_id 6), Sales, traveling in Lisbon. Triage flagged user_blocked=true, but lookup_user shows sign_in_blocked=false, status active, vpn_access=true, failed_login_count=0. Discrepancy with triage noted; no block is in place. Duo push enrolled (duo_push, phone). Sign-in logs: last 14 days show 10 successful sign-ins, 0 failed_password, 0 mfa_denied. VPN successes from Lisbon on Oct 8, 9, 10 (residential IP 198.51.100.66, Duo push). No failed attempts logged, so today's failure may not be reaching the server. Likely cause: hotel Wi-Fi sign-in page not accepted, or client needs restart (KB-013 fix 4 and 3). Action taken: none requiring approval. No password reset, unlock, or block requested. Next step if user reports failure with an error: check for failed attempts in logs and escalate per KB-013 'Escalate when' (account and Duo fine, attempts reach server, still fails). Consider whether the failed attempt is logged at all, since logs show no failures.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-013",
    "KB-015"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
